      "lineNbr": 268,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000043
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-10T15:25:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will *silently* remove the most-significant bit of the major revision number. Although I understand why you\u0027re doing this (because the doc says this bit is RES0!), I wonder whether this is the right thing to do, or whether this should be treated as an error. We could define proper types for a major (and a minor) version number instead of simply using `u16`, and enforce by construction that a `RmmMajorVersion` value always has bit#15 as zero.\n\nI am not saying this is necessarily the right thing to do but wondered if you had considered this and had any thoughts around that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 268,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 268,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "03668d004fca88bca81dfbe23dac78401ea38f1b",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d466caf_4ca3b827",
        "filename": "src/services/rmmd/manifest.rs",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000043
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-10T15:25:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If `self` got constructed through `RmmBootManifestVersion::new()` then there should not be any need to mask out bit#31 because it should already be zero by construction. I guess there is an issue if instead `self` comes from an integer conversion? But then I suppose we could implement the `From`/`Into` traits to enforce that as well?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 272,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 272,
        "endChar": 30
